<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One column of italic verse, centred on the page, with the printed signature line in capitals below it. No running head, page number or notes.</layout>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Latioque Patrioque Tullio humectat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Et invidendis uberat favis linguam,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Fandi potentem quando suspicit magnas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Hiante &amp; aure &amp; ore devorans voces</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Iuuenta totis destinata diuinis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Tantoque coetus, si bonum suum novit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Felix Magistro, &amp; insolente famosi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Monitore Recti. Pande mentis augustos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Doctor recessus. Vindica fidem Vero,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Lumen Lyceo, gloriam ingeni fama,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Scientiam Orbi, Conscientiam Caelo.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Iam vindicasti. Laudibus tuis ecce</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Subscribit Aether, docta natio applaudit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Invitus atrum Livor atterit dentem,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Reddunt honorem idonei aestimatores,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Faventque linguis; vilis umbra post omnes,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Meus Tuarum cultor ille virtutum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Litatque farre simplici, indisertumque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Ineruditus carmen adstrepit Scazon:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Et pro salute, pro laboribus longum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Superstitandis [?], grande, rite quod vortat!</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>At impetrabile, ore suscipit votum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Ut sospitem Aether commodet diu terris</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Patriaque profuturum; ut oris ac mentis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Non poenitendos illa demetat fructus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>In posterumque sero discat absentem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Quaesisse chartis, tunc Sionios inter</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Scriptum Quirites, Caelitum Senatorem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>Sine hac Tibi accini, Professor, &amp; nostrae</i>
    </l>
    <l n="30">
      <i>Interpretare gratitudinis partem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="31">
      <i>Quas candidus conatur, o genus Divum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="32">
      <i>Amor loquelas. Cernitis? polo late</i>
    </l>
    <l n="33">
      <i>Nitor emicat praesagus. Annuit votis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="34">
      <i>Virtus Olympi, longiusque Te nobis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="35">
      <i>Servare velle, Te decoris exemplum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="36">
      <i>Animanque. Ipsa, Livor hoc audi,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="37">
      <i>Aeternitatis Diva praestes &amp; famam,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="38">
      <i>Felicibus quae dat libris perremare,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="39">
      <i>Rerumque trux vorator omnium Tempus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="40">
      <i>Genium hisce Scriptis, inclytamque &amp;</i>
    </l>
    <l n="41">
      <i>ingentem Laude usque germinante praestat aetatem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="42" para="true">ISACUS TREUGHORN, <i>Dantiscanus.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The verse is set without visible stanza breaks, so it is given as one paragraph. Some words are uncertain in the scan: "Superstitandis" is marked [?]. The signature line is set in capitals but is a name, so it is a paragraph, not a heading.</notes>
</page>
